# Product-docs house style

This repo holds Extole's customer-facing documentation, built on Mintlify. Merging to
`main` publishes docs.extole.com, so a merge is a publish.

**Before you write or edit any page under `guides/`, `product/`, `technical/`, `news/`, or
`runbooks/`, read [`.mintlify/AGENTS.md`](../../.mintlify/AGENTS.md).** It is where every
writing standard for this repo is defined — voice, terminology, structure, formatting,
links, images, frontmatter, accuracy — and each rule is stated there in full rather than
referenced, so applying it needs no other file. Apply it in the same edit, before human
review; reviewers should be spending their time on substance, not on the same wording
corrections every time.

That file is a distillation of the docs team's Google Docs and a fork of the same standards
in `extole/product-docs-readme`; it carries a **Provenance** section saying which copy wins
and when the others are worth opening. Nothing you need in order to *write* a page lives
outside it.

It is the canonical copy for a reason: Mintlify's own agent reads it directly, and it
cannot follow links. Any standard that lives somewhere else is a standard that some
editing surface silently ignores. So when a rule changes, change it there — not here, and
not in a skill.

## Three guardrails that apply even if you read nothing else

- **Never invent product behavior, event names, metrics, or numbers** to make prose flow.
  Verify against the platform, or say you are unsure. Plausible-sounding fiction is the
  most expensive error possible in customer docs.
- **Never rewrite a literal.** Event names (`promotion clicked`, `converted`), schema
  fields (`step_name`), API identifiers, and code samples are real values, not style
  targets.
- **Never add a remote image URL**, and never one carrying an `expires=` parameter. Images
  are repo assets under `images/`, referenced root-relative.

## Process is elsewhere

Validation, previews, branches, pull requests, and reviewer comments are not style. See the
`product-docs-placement`, `product-docs-authoring`, and `mintlify-branch-preview` skills
in `.agents/skills/`. Load `product-docs-placement` before writing a new page — Guides
is not the default tab.
